  "title": "NVIDIA Halts AI Chip Shipments to Southeast Asia Amid U.S. AI Restrictions",
  "summary": "NVIDIA has halted shipments of AI servers to four Southeast Asian countries after the U.S. imposes stricter export controls on advanced AI chips, including a new list of entities requiring a government license for sales of such technology.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "NVIDIA halted shipments of AI servers to Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand, and Indonesia.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. added NVIDIA's Megaspeed to its Entity List, requiring a government license for sales of advanced AI chips.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang returned as CEO, highlighting the broader implications of U.S. trade controls on the global AI race.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
